@startuml
actor User
participant FE
participant BE
participant DB

User -> FE : Request file download

FE -> BE : GET /files/{id}
BE -> BE : Validate JWT
BE -> DB : Fetch ciphertext + wrapped_FEK\n+ nonce + auth_tag + stored_hash\n+ enc_algo + hash_algo
DB --> BE : encrypted file data
BE --> FE : encrypted file data

note over FE : All decryption happens\nclient-side only

FE -> FE : Prompt user for password
FE -> FE : Derive key from password (PBKDF2)
FE -> FE : Decrypt private key blob → RSA key object
FE -> FE : Unwrap FEK using RSA private key (OAEP)
FE -> FE : Decrypt ciphertext using FEK\n(AES-256-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305)
FE -> FE : Verify auth tag (tamper check on ciphertext)

FE -> FE : Recompute hash of decrypted plaintext\n(using stored hash_algo)
FE -> FE : Compare recomputed hash vs stored hash

alt hashes match
    FE --> User : Plaintext file + INTEGRITY PASS
else hashes differ
    FE --> User : Warning — file integrity FAILED\n(possible tampering detected)
end
@enduml